      "get": {
        "operationId": "facet-offense-summary",
        "summary": "League-wide offense summary leaderboard",
        "description": "Every qualifying player in the league, with their offensive snaps, production and grades. Two\ncomplete requests exist: `--league` with `--season` (a year, or a comma-separated list such as\n`2023,2024`), or `--game` alone (an id from `ref-games`) — anything less is refused with `400\ninvalid_parameter`. Narrow with `--week` and `--franchise`. `--division` fans the request out across\nNCAA divisions and is ignored for every other league. Grades are on PFF's 0-100 scale and every\nother column is a raw total or rate; which columns come back depends on the report, the position and\nthe caller's entitlement. Add `--export true` for the raw CSV instead of JSON.\n\nThis export has no header row and one blank line per record, so the export is one blank line per row\nwith no header row.\n\nA present-but-empty `league`, `season` or `week` short-circuits to an empty 200.\n\nWith `export=true` the response is `text/csv` as an attachment named `download.csv` instead of JSON.",
