        "operationId": "team-rushing-direction",
        "summary": "A team's rushing by direction, one row per rusher and gap, plus totals",
        "description": "Two tables in one answer. `columns` and `rows` hold one row per rusher and run direction — the\nplayer's id, name and position, the direction (left end to right end, then the quarterback\nbuckets) and the eleven direction stats: attempts, yards, yards per attempt, touchdowns, first\ndowns, explosive runs, yards after contact and per attempt, longest, avoided tackles, fumbles.\nRushers are ordered by total attempts, most first, so the first rows are the lead back.\n`totalsColumns` and `teamTotals` hold one row per direction for the whole team. `season`\ndefaults to the current season and `weekGroup` to `REGPO`. Served for NCAA programmes the same\nway; a programme with no rows in that source gets both tables empty rather than an error. A\nreport that takes longer than a minute may come back with fewer columns than usual — rerun it.\nWith `format=csv` the rusher × direction table streams as a file, or the team totals with\n`table=totals`; see `CsvTable`.",
        "tags": [
          "team"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/LeaguePath"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TeamPath"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/SeasonQuery"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/WeekGroupQuery"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/FormatQuery"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TableQuery"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The two tables.",
            "headers": {
              "Content-Disposition": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/CsvContentDisposition"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TeamRushingDirectionTable"
                }
              },
              "text/csv": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CsvTable"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          },
          "429": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/RateLimited"
          },
          "500": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/InternalError"
          },
          "502": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/UpstreamError"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/UpstreamUnavailable"
          },
          "504": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/UpstreamTimeout"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v2/{league}/teams/{team}/reports/{report}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "team-report",
        "summary": "One of nineteen player reports for a team, one row per player",
        "description": "The team's players in one report — `passing`, `rushing`, `coverage`, `punting` and the rest —\none row per player with the report's own stat columns. Which columns come back depends on the\nreport, the season and the entitlement, so `columns` names and types them per answer rather than\nthis document enumerating them; the three identity keys `playerId`, `player` and `position` are\nalways present. `season` defaults to the current season and `weekGroup` to `REGPO`; `week` and\n`weekTo` narrow the group to one week or a span. The five special-teams reports start in the\n2013 season; an earlier season is refused with `400 invalid_parameter`. Served for NCAA\nprogrammes the same way; a report with no rows for the programme in its section comes back\nas an empty table, never an error. A report that takes longer than a minute may come back\nwith fewer columns than usual — rerun it. With `format=csv` the table streams as a file; see\n`CsvTable`.",
        "tags": [
          "team"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/LeaguePath"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TeamPath"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TeamReportPath"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/SeasonQuery"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/WeekGroupQuery"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/WeekQuery"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/WeekToQuery"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/FormatQuery"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The table.",
            "headers": {
              "Content-Disposition": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/CsvContentDisposition"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TeamReportTable"
                }
              },
              "text/csv": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CsvTable"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
