            "string",
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "CsvTable": {
        "title": "CsvTable",
        "description": "The table as a file, when `format=csv`. Four rules: the first line is the column keys in\n`columns` order and every following line is one row, lines end in CRLF; a field holding a\ncomma, a double quote, CR or LF is wrapped in double quotes with embedded quotes doubled\n(RFC 4180); a `null` cell is an empty field, booleans are `true`/`false`, numbers print exactly\nas they do in the JSON body (no rounding, no thousands separators); the file is UTF-8 with no\nbyte-order mark. An empty table is the header line alone. Metadata that sits beside the table\nin the JSON body is not in the file.",
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1,
        "pattern": "^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*(,[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*)*\\r\\n"
      },
      "TeamStatsRow": {
        "title": "TeamStatsRow",
        "description": "One team. `teamId`, `abbreviation` and `name` are always present; every other key is a stat value\nor its rank, named by `columns`. A stat that does not apply to the team is `null`, and so is a\nrank the scope has no answer for.",
